2186045417] [17592186531556 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531556 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531556 #edb/ref 1077 "field-7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531556 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186531301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531556 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff58c76f-d503-592c-8830-047604f3389f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332913" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+$ {{field-1}} $\\cdot \\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e73d348-8d9b-5a9f-8dbf-5305290f7f53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531575 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-3{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -3[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3a \\\\ -3b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2b \\\\ 2a\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-3a \\\\ -3b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2b+1 \\\\ 2a+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2b+1=-3a \\\\ 2a+5=-3b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n-2b+1=-3a\\,⇒\\,a=\\frac{2b-1}{3}.\n$$\n\n \nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n2(\\frac{2b-1}{3})+5=-3b\\,⇒\\,4b-2+15=-9b\\,⇒\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\na=\\frac{2(-1)-1}{3}=\\frac{-2-1}{3}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-333012" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system is\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,{t}^{2}+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    $2$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    $\\,\\,t+\\,\\,$\n  </td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">\n    .\n  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n    $1$\n  </td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3234de52-8801-51a2-806f-23f965c5de2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531578 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1} \\\\ {b}_{2}\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1},{c}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-({a}_{2}{t}^{2}+{b}_{2}t+{c}_{2}) \\\\ {a}_{1}{t}^{2}+{b}_{1}t+{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{2}+t+3 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{1}t+{b}_{1} \\\\ 0{t}^{2}+2{a}_{2}t+{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-{a}_{2}+2){t}^{2}+(-{b}_{2}+1)t+(-{c}_{2}+3) \\\\ ({a}_{1}-1){t}^{2}+({b}_{1}+2)t+{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding coefficients of like powers of $t,$ we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{2}+2=0 \\\\ -\\,{b}_{2}+1=2{a}_{1} \\\\ -\\,{c}_{2}+3={b}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1}-1=0 \\\\ {b}_{1}+2=2{a}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}={b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first and fourth equations, we get\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=2,\\,{a}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the second and fifth equations, and solving for ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n{b}_{2}=-1,\\,{b}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting these last values into the third and sixth equations, and solving for ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=1,\\,{c}_{1}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+2t-1 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}-t+1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{t}^{2}+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2/5 & -6/5 \\\\ -6/5 & -7/5\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38450a0f-4d09-5bde-a910-db2e5f9dab01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531581 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332587" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531590 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2