 align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-5}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-6}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-7}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-8}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56f780de-76f1-5a1a-81ae-abc4bc467c3f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531594 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite our system, highlighting the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=(-2)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{4t}\\cdot 5+{e}^{5t}\\cdot 0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)+1\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)+{e}^{4t}\\cdot 0+{e}^{5t}\\cdot 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in matrix form:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{5t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332746" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following inhomogeneous system of linear differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nA complementary solution to this system is given by\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}(t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]){e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThen, the general solution of the system can be written as \n$x(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t),$\nwhere ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution. Determine the form of the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86e2d08a-1bef-5ead-ab02-f3370f825b7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531615 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also constant, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ are constants that are to be determined." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531454 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186531500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1069 "q-332585" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186531652 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe systems of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as